# AGENT.md — src/presentation/

The outermost layer. Fastify plugins that convert HTTP requests into application
service calls and return HTTP responses.

## What lives here

- `<module>/routes.ts` — exports a default Fastify plugin function
  (`export default async function(fastify: FastifyInstance)`).
  Creates its own repository/service instances and registers routes.

## Rules

1. Route plugins call application services, never repositories directly.
2. Each plugin exports one default async function. `app.ts` registers it with
   `await fastify.register(moduleRoutes, { prefix: '/name' })`.
3. Inside the plugin, routes are registered with `fastify.get()`,
   `fastify.post()`, etc.
4. Responses use `reply.status(code).send(data)`.
5. Error handling is done globally via `setErrorHandler` in `app.ts`.
   Throw `AppError` subclasses for expected client errors.
6. When adding a new module, register its plugin in `src/app.ts`.
